extends /views/templates/layouts/_base

append variables
	- pagetitle = "How it works"
	- pagedescription = "How Tablechart turns a table into a chart, and when the chart builds."

block content
	.lane
		.container
			.page-header
				h1 How it works
				p.lead How a table becomes a chart, and when the chart builds.

	+section("From table to chart")
		p When you call #[code init()], Tablechart finds every element with #[code data-chart]. It reads the table in it: the first cell of a row is the label, the other cells are values. Then it adds the chart to the element.
		p The table stays in the page, hidden from view. Screen readers read it, and a translation script finds the labels in it.

	+section("When a chart builds")
		p A chart builds when it scrolls into view. By default, half of the chart must be in view. Set #[code threshold] to change that, from #[code 0] to #[code 1].
		p If #[code replay] is #[code true], a chart builds again each time it scrolls back into view. If not, it builds once.

		+codeblock('JS').
			init({
			  threshold: 0.5,
			  replay: false
			});

	+section("Inside an animated container")
		p If a chart is inside an element that animates in, for example with a CSS animation, the chart builds when that animation is halfway. Then the chart builds in a container that can already be seen. See #[a(href=url('/features/animated-parents.html')) Animated parents].

	+section("Text")
		p All text in a chart is HTML: the title, the names and the numbers. It uses the font of the page. Only the bars, lines and slices are SVG.

	+section("Size")
		p A chart fills the width of its container. Its height is a share of its width, set with #[code data-chart-aspect], but never less than #[code --tablechart-min-height], 200px by default. If the width changes, the chart is laid out again.

	+section("Reduced motion and print")
		p If the visitor prefers reduced motion, charts build without animation. When the page is printed, every chart is shown whole.

	+section("Accessibility")
		p Screen readers read the table, not the drawing. See #[a(href=url('/features/accessibility.html')) Accessibility].

	+section("Next")
		p See #[a(href=url('/get-started.html')) Get started] to add Tablechart to your page.

	hr
	section.no-hr
		.container
			+anchor(title="Support this project")
			p Tablechart is free. If it saved you time, a coffee goes a long way.

			a.btn.solid.chevron(href="https://ko-fi.com/martinomagnifico" target="_blank" rel="noopener")
				+coffee()
				| Support my work on Ko-fi
				+chevron()



